<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charSet="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><link rel="preload" as="image" href="/images/ThePoolLab.png"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css" crossorigin="" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="preload" as="script" fetchPriority="low" href="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin=""/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/fd9d1056-4dbbcf07a05c3f48.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/472-6eced84fcf03e6a3.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/main-app-ce281d8555633725.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/975-95592eb349967368.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/app/layout-4ee2f436a51b65f2.js" async=""></script><title>Dolphin Nautilus Titan vs Aiper Scuba S1: Which Smart Pool Cleaner Is Better? - The Pool Lab</title><meta name="description" content="Compare the Dolphin Nautilus Titan and Aiper Scuba S1 across smart features, cordless convenience, cleaning performance, wall climbing, and long-term value."/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/blog/dolphin-nautilus-titan-vs-aiper-scuba-s1"/><meta property="og:title" content="Dolphin Nautilus Titan vs Aiper Scuba S1: Which Smart Pool Cleaner Is Better?"/><meta property="og:description" content="Compare the Dolphin Nautilus Titan and Aiper Scuba S1 across smart features, cordless convenience, cleaning performance, wall climbing, and long-term value."/><meta property="og:type" content="article"/><meta property="article:published_time" content="2026-06-03"/><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><meta name="twitter:title" content="The Pool Lab - Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:description" content="Your ultimate guide to Robot Pool Cleaners, reviews, and maintenance tips."/><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://www.the-pool-lab.com/images/ThePoolLabOG.png"/><script src="/_next/static/chunks/polyfills-c67a75d1b6f99dc8.js" crossorigin="" noModule=""></script></head><body class="d-flex flex-column min-vh-100"><nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-light bg-light"><div class="container"><a class="navbar-brand d-flex align-items-center" href="/"><div style="width:160px;height:90px;position:relative;margin-right:10px"><img src="/images/ThePoolLab.png" alt="The Pool Lab Logo" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain"/></div><span class="d-none d-sm-inline">The Pool Lab</span></a><button class="navbar-toggler" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#navbarNav"><span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span></button><div class="collapse navbar-collapse" id="navbarNav"><ul class="navbar-nav ms-auto"><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/">Home</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/reviews">Reviews</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/best-of">Best of</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/guides">Guides</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link" href="/about">About</a></li></ul></div></div></nav><main class="flex-grow-1"><div class="container my-5"><nav aria-label="breadcrumb"><ol class="breadcrumb"><li class="breadcrumb-item"><a href="/">Home</a></li><li class="breadcrumb-item active" aria-current="page">Blog</li></ol></nav><article><h1 class="mb-4">Dolphin Nautilus Titan vs Aiper Scuba S1: Which Smart Pool Cleaner Is Better?</h1><p class="text-muted mb-5">Posted on <!-- -->2026-06-03</p><div class="row"><div class="col-lg-8"><div><h2>Quick Verdict</h2><p>The <strong>Dolphin Nautilus Titan</strong> is the better option for buyers who want connected features, reliable cleaning, and strong wall coverage from an established robotic pool cleaner platform.</p><p>The <strong>Aiper Scuba S1</strong> is better for buyers who want a cordless cleaner that is easy to drop in, remove, charge, and store.</p><h2>At-a-Glance Comparison</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Dolphin Nautilus Titan</th><th>Aiper Scuba S1</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Power Style</td><td>Corded</td><td>Cordless</td></tr><tr><td>App Control</td><td>Yes</td><td>Model dependent</td></tr><tr><td>Wall Cleaning</td><td>Excellent</td><td>Good</td></tr><tr><td>Runtime</td><td>Continuous</td><td>Battery limited</td></tr><tr><td>Handling</td><td>Very Good</td><td>Excellent</td></tr><tr><td>Best For</td><td>Reliable smart cleaning</td><td>Cordless convenience</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Cleaning Performance</h2><p>The Nautilus Titan has the edge in cleaning consistency. Its corded design allows longer cycles and more predictable coverage, especially in larger pools.</p><p>The Aiper Scuba S1 is easier to handle and simpler to deploy, but cordless convenience comes with runtime limits. For smaller or moderate-size pools, that may not be a problem. For larger or debris-heavy pools, the Titan is safer.</p><h2>Ease of Ownership</h2><p>Aiper wins on physical convenience. No cord means no untangling, no power supply placement, and less setup friction. The Titan wins on dependable automation, stronger wall performance, and broader pool compatibility.</p><h2>Final Recommendation</h2><p>Choose the <strong>Nautilus Titan</strong> if you want the better all-around cleaner. Choose the <strong>Aiper Scuba S1</strong> if cordless convenience matters more than maximum cleaning consistency.</p><h2>Related Resources</h2><ul><li><a href='/reviews/Dolphin-Nautilus-Titan'>Dolphin Nautilus Titan Review</a></li><li><a href='/reviews/Aiper-Scuba-S1'>Aiper Scuba S1 Review</a></li><li><a href='/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-aiper-scuba-s1'>Nautilus CC Plus vs Aiper Scuba S1</a></li><li><a href='/blog/corded-vs-cordless-robotic-pool-cleaners'>Corded vs Cordless Robotic Pool Cleaners</a></li></ul><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h3>Which cleaner is better for wall climbing?</h3><p>The Nautilus Titan generally has the advantage for wall climbing and waterline consistency.</p><h3>Which is easier to use?</h3><p>The Aiper Scuba S1 is easier to handle because it is cordless, but the Titan is more capable overall.</p></div><div class="mt-5"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/reviews">Find Your Perfect Robot</a></div></div></div></article></div></main><footer class="bg-dark text-white text-center py-3 mt-auto"><div class="container"><p class="mb-1">© <!-- -->2026<!-- --> <!-- -->The Pool Lab<!-- -->. All rights reserved.</p><small class="text-white-50">The Pool Lab<!-- --> is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com.</small></div></footer><script src="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin="" async=""></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0]);self.__next_f.push([2,null])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1:HL[\"/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n2:HL[\"/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n0:\"$L3\"\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"4:I[3728,[],\"\"]\n6:I[9928,[],\"\"]\n7:I[8326,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"308\",\"static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js\"],\"\"]\n8:I[6954,[],\"\"]\n9:I[7264,[],\"\"]\nc:I[5826,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"308\",\"static/chunks/app/blog/%5Bslug%5D/page-23a4c3f098b125a3.js\"],\"\"]\nd:I[7625,[\"326\",\"static/chunks/326-bff252670b7455ef.js\",\"975\",\"static/chunks/97