tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003ch2\u003eCleaning Performance\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Nautilus Titan has the edge in cleaning consistency. Its corded design allows longer cycles and more predictable coverage, especially in larger pools.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Aiper Scuba S1 is easier to handle and simpler to deploy, but cordless convenience comes with runtime limits. For smaller or moderate-size pools, that may not be a problem. For larger or debris-heavy pools, the Titan is safer.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eEase of Ownership\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eAiper wins on physical convenience. No cord means no untangling, no power supply placement, and less setup friction. The Titan wins on dependable automation, stronger wall performance, and broader pool compatibility.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eFinal Recommendation\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eChoose the \u003cstrong\u003eNautilus Titan\u003c/strong\u003e if you want the better all-around cleaner. Choose the \u003cstrong\u003eAiper Scuba S1\u003c/strong\u003e if cordless convenience matters more than maximum cleaning consistency.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2\u003eRelated Resources\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/reviews/Dolphin-Nautilus-Titan'\u003eDolphin Nautilus Titan Review\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/reviews/Aiper-Scuba-S1'\u003eAiper Scuba S1 Review\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/blog/dolphin-nautilus-cc-plus-vs-aiper-scuba-s1'\u003eNautilus CC Plus vs Aiper Scuba S1\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href='/blog/corded-vs-cordless-robotic-pool-cleaners'\u003eCorded vs Cordless Robotic Pool Cleaners\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch2\u003eFrequently Asked Questions\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWhich cleaner is better for wall climbing?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Nautilus Titan generally has the advantage for wall climbing and waterline consistency.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch3\u003eWhich is easier to use?\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Aiper Scuba S1 is easier to handle because it is cordless, but the Titan is more capable overall.\u003c/p\u003e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"3:[[[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"1\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]],[\"$\",\"$L4\",null,{\"buildId\":\"ibMnxLVRNd6eQkSmhgFst\",\"assetPrefix\":\"\",\"initialCanonicalUrl\":\"/blog/dolphin-nautilus-titan-vs-aiper-scuba-s1\",\"initialTree\":[\"\",{\"children\":[\"blog\",{\"children\":[[\"slug\",\"dolphin-nautilus-titan-vs-aiper-scuba-s1\",\"d\"],{\"children\":[\"__PAGE__?{\\\"slug\\\":\\\"dolphin-nautilus-titan-vs-aiper-scuba-s1\\\"}\",{}]}]}]},\"$undefined\",\"$undefined\",true],\"initialHead\":[false,\"$L5\"],\"globalErrorComponent\":\"$6\",\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"html\",null,{\"lang\":\"en\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"body\",null,{\"className\":\"d-flex flex-column min-vh-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"className\":\"navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-light bg-light\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"container\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L7\",null,{\"href\":\"/\",\"className\":\"navbar-brand d-flex align-items-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"style\":{\"width\":\"160px\",\"height\":\"90px\",\"position\":\"relative\",\"marginRight\":\"10px\"},\"children\":[\"$\",\"img\",null,{\"src\":\"/images/ThePoolLab.png\",\"alt\":\"The Pool Lab Logo\",\"style\":{\"width\":\"100%\",\"height\":\"100%\",\"objectFit\":\"contain\"}}]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"d-none d-sm-inline\",\"children\":\"The Pool Lab\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"button\",null,{\"className\":\"navbar-toggler\",\"type\":\"button\",\"data-bs-toggle\":\"collapse\",\"data-bs-target\":\"#navbarNav\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"navbar-toggler-icon\"